{"title":"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> distinct points on the positive\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis be joined to each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> distinct points on\nthe positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis. Assume no three segments\nare concurrent (except at the axes). Obtain\nwith proof a formula for the number of interior\nintersection points. The diagram shows that\nthe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904f27995d33e0d39f43ec959e7cb100516e9396.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/a/90ad4595d51deba0bbcd7e99759644e4faf9acde.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2.$\" width=\"47\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/4/9a4f1e83e4540dd6d84dee9c1a84b446076fed15.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] draw((0,0)--(0,3),arrow=Arrow()); draw((0,0)--(4,0),arrow=Arrow()); for(int x=0;x&lt;4;++x){ for(int y=0;y&lt;3;++y){ D((x,0)--(0,y),black); }} dot(IP((2,0)--(0,1),(1,0)--(0,2))); dot(IP((3,0)--(0,1),(1,0)--(0,2))); dot(IP((3,0)--(0,1),(2,0)--(0,2))); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"192\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Notice that choosing two points on the x axis and two points on the y axis, then, after constructing all possible lines, there will be only one point of intersection. So the answer is \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738548af079240e1a65cdc413bb068ce22ea8bc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{m}{2} \\binom{n}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"79\" height=\"53\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the points be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2bfdf07c873dc80b35ec716c310cb45881fa74c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_1 &lt; x_2 \\dots &lt; x_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"133\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/3094abc5895b9820a3941478909eec0d84800079.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y_1&lt;y_2 \\dots &lt; y_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/0/6808e74a067e64c2029f6b3475e0f345a54ba676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i,y_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> represent the segment formed by joining <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/8/f4833b0dceb1e08847fedacceea92a28de10a3ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i,0), (0,y_j)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" />. We first take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/5/b354638f824de285dce6d6d3f72163cb287aeff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" />. No segments intersect this. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbbfe28176e2103d1c752d07f9c1371d2ed74ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, all the segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/3/7c34bc0a4503a262b95c5c70fc896cbbcb06e12a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i,y_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />,  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/1/be1ddb99be68b74170679d41ee6b9e5412708f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i \\in \\{2,3 \\dots m\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" /> will intersect. Thus, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/5/595b8a762af5611ae35ee2d55be5bd7f4d7a2da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-1)(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" /> intersections. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591a1b674ac9db57f824fe9693cf11b102fbd540.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"20\" />, all the segments with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/7/d67a2201deb86d684a6d970bf5156b58e25db269.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_i,y_1),(x_i,y_2), x_i \\neq x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" /> will intersect this. Thus we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/8/5a88077fa9d10b7147319730d4ea7c427c44ccce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-1)(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"86\" height=\"20\" /> intersections. We keep going like this and finally for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/8/2f8879032956c696d6aa42384674cb673aa95efe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_1,y_n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"60\" height=\"20\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/9/ca91610b3193fb6ef91d90651874957de88fa2ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-1)(n-1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"120\" height=\"20\" /> intersections. When we move to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/a/d8a273c51708d0f8f2102f4996ccc81d1bb50b1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_2,y_i)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, we note that only points to the right intersect, thus we will be doing the same steps with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/e/0be0ccfd88520759f46cecf340fc384f523c68f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(m-2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> instead. From this, we get the total intersections to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9011fd70b1ef7b21950dcb42f7c657aff4b257.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(1 + 2 + \\dots +  n-1)(m-1) + (1 + 2 + \\dots + n-1)(m-2) \\dots (1 + 2 + \\dots +  n-1)(1) = \\boxed{\\frac{(n-1)(n)}{2} \\cdot \\frac{(m-1)(m)}{2}}\\]\" width=\"790\" height=\"50\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II\">2009 UNCO Math Contest II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://uncmathcontest.wordpress.com/\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_UNCO_Math_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 UNCO Math Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=University_of_Northern_Colorado_Math_Contest\" title=\"University of Northern Colorado Math Contest\"> All UNCO Math Contest Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017222024\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.025 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.041 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 194/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1407/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 94/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5017/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.143      1 Template:UNCO_Math_Contest_box\n100.00%    7.143      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:13504:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017222024 and revision id 259113. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}